# nextpnr-himbaechel (router2) diverging on crack2_glyph_top.sv
#
# Captured from a synth,pnr run of crack2_glyph_m6 (retime 100, timing_margin 6) on the
# xc7vx485t.  The configurable-alphabet engine stores its glyph table as an 896-bit flop
# vector (code[7*128-1:0]) read by MAXLEN parallel 128:1 part-select muxes (key formation
# and hit reporting) and written by a variable-index 128-way demux (the scanner).  That is
# a large, densely-connected combinational cloud with very high fanout on the table net, and
# the router cannot resolve its congestion.
#
# The negotiated-congestion router descends to a MINIMUM at iter 8 (overused = 5188), then
# turns around and climbs monotonically -- the classic non-convergence / "oscillation then
# divergence" signature.  Left to run it churns indefinitely without producing a bitstream.
#
# The fix is exactly what the mask-vs-table discussion concluded: hold the glyph table in a
# real RAM (an unpacked array that the mapper infers as LUTRAM, with replicated read ports),
# not a flop vector read by muxes.  This file is kept as a reproducible demonstration of the
# router's divergence behaviour.
#
# iter / wires routed / overused wires:
iter=1 wires=499256 overused=41404 overuse=45092
iter=2 wires=530053 overused=19186 overuse=19473
iter=3 wires=540579 overused=10878 overuse=10952
iter=4 wires=547495 overused=7481 overuse=7498
iter=5 wires=552311 overused=5994 overuse=6012
iter=6 wires=555630 overused=5459 overuse=5481
iter=7 wires=558743 overused=5202 overuse=5215
iter=8 wires=561768 overused=5188 overuse=5197   <-- minimum; router cannot clear the basin
iter=9 wires=565150 overused=5355 overuse=5374   <-- turns around
iter=10 wires=567876 overused=5616 overuse=5630
iter=11 wires=570440 overused=6055 overuse=6077
iter=12 wires=572898 overused=6487 overuse=6506
iter=13 wires=576679 overused=7206 overuse=7224
iter=14 wires=580299 overused=7947 overuse=7986
iter=15 wires=583882 overused=8827 overuse=8880
iter=16 wires=587826 overused=9807 overuse=9862
iter=17 wires=591891 overused=10626 overuse=10679
iter=18 wires=595648 overused=11422 overuse=11473   <-- diverging; killed here
